summary:
M4's code and tests hold. The build scores exactly like the S3 prototype:
- every E-S3 vector, golden and hash I re-derived matches;
- the 24 frozen timelines judge at the shipped run-1 scores;
- 15 pinned L3 configurations re-run independently on the prototype equal the notes and the pins.

A clean copy passes `verify --quick` (847 pass, luau-lsp 0 errors), plain L3 for M4 passes (170 pass, 159 s), and a sample of the volume cases passes with their pinned values. M4's L1 share is 2.0-2.2 s by the runner at 44 % busy. The volume tier, its refusals and its self-test work as L5 states (5 of 5 runner mutants caught). The fingerprint re-bless covers only D3's two rows. No §6.4 rule is broken, and no decodable timeline crashed or gave NaN in 450 fuzzed ones.

pass is false because of two text-only majors under L11:
1. The handoff's new §6.4 rule 2 says "no other math member", which would make the SPEC false for the code's uses of `math.huge`; it also contradicts the handoff's own T-META-03 row.
2. The handoff and notes claim HoldZone's two fire-decay groupings give the same doubles at 600, so the pin "matters only if a retune moves the value". In fact 0.10 % of uniform F differ, and regrouping the build fails plain L3's parity checks; the original experiment's LCG has only 23 fraction bits.

Both fixes are one-sentence rewrites, applied in my copy.

The minors:
- missing **[Decision to confirm]** marks for O13 and O14 in the SPEC text;
- two test gaps found by mutation (the Exact bot's D7 clock, autoplay's "due by t"), each with an added assertion tried in my copy;
- an overstated L3V rationale (Reference covers only the human players; the Perfect HoldZone bot is pinned by L3V alone);
- several wording or number nits.

I did not run slices 9-11 (the lead's) or T-PERF-02. Files are in C:\Users\louis\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\C--Users-louis-Documents-RANDOM-ROBLOX\93ae48b4-72b9-4dc1-aa5d-451af1abf9a0\scratchpad\m4-v2-1:
